{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538030714,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4NzAxOTk3ODQ="},"added":["waiting-for-directmode-death"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1538048632,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNTA1OTUwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2877#issuecomment-425059502"},"message":"Since it looks like v6 support is at the very least not worse ATM and annex itself solved some issues, making possible to improve at our side, I agree. We should ensure v6 to be the default on \"crippled FS\", since this is not (yet) the case for annex itself. This should be the first step and second disabling the test builds. Third, remove a lot of code and fourth work on better support for v6.\nHowever, I have no really strong opinion regarding the order of the first two steps. I do see the argument for disabling tests being more urgent. But it shouldn't lead to us forgetting about the other one for a too long time ...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538060217,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNTEyNDYzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2877#issuecomment-425124639"},"message":"@chrislfilo You are the most dedicated Windows user we have, and you previously reported success with using datalad to get some datasets.  Have you tried to do anything beyond getting datasets on Windows? Or you did, it didn't work and you just gave up on trying...?\n\n@mih is pushing for dropping support for 'direct' mode of operation on windows in favor of v6 mode.  Both are IMHO largely workarounds for the fact of absent symlinks etc on Windows file systems. direct mode is the initial, really crude workaround, where v6 is much better and more inline with git and seamless operation.\n\nIf you are keen to try v6 mode of operation, you could `set DATALAD_REPO_VERSION=6` in your Windows shell and try to do all the regular `datalad install/get/save/add/...` and see how it goes.  It all should largely (there are corners... but much more functional than original \"direct\" mode) be functional already if you have recent git-annex.\n\nYou feedback would be invaluable to instruct our direction to take.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538060217,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzNDQ5MDMxNg=="},"target":"14bc09229bde2bd523996b12f47ce2382fa304f06080b91f280960b61a0b70aa","message":"@chrisfilo You are the most dedicated Windows user we have, and you previously reported success with using datalad to get some datasets.  Have you tried to do anything beyond getting datasets on Windows? Or you did, it didn't work and you just gave up on trying...?\n\n@mih is pushing for dropping support for 'direct' mode of operation on windows in favor of v6 mode.  Both are IMHO largely workarounds for the fact of absent symlinks etc on Windows file systems. direct mode is the initial, really crude workaround, where v6 is much better and more inline with git and seamless operation.\n\nIf you are keen to try v6 mode of operation, you could `set DATALAD_REPO_VERSION=6` in your Windows shell and try to do all the regular `datalad install/get/save/add/...` and see how it goes.  It all should largely (there are corners... but much more functional than original \"direct\" mode) be functional already if you have recent git-annex.\n\nYou feedback would be invaluable to instruct our direction to take.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538066426,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNTE2MTI3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2877#issuecomment-425161276"},"message":"`git config --global --add datalad.repo.version 6`","files":null},{"typ